<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14443" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dis-sŭo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, ūtum,
			3, v. a.—<b>Lit.</b>,
				<i>to unstitich</i>, <i>to rip
			open;</i> hence, in gen., <i>to</i>
			
			<i>open</i>, <i>to dissolve by
			degrees</i> (a rare word). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					1, 408</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malas,</span>”
				<i>to open the mouth wide</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					3, 59</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">habebit vestimenta dissuta, caput nudum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Levit. 13, 45</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amicitiae dissuendae magis quam discindendae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Lael. 21, 76</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sensim amicitias (opp. repente praecidere),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Off. 1, 33, 120</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
